Round 5 complete. The decisive discovery this round was the **structural insight in `inputevents`** (the same class of finding that cracked the round-1 rules).

## Key new rule: order-segment duration (E9)

MIMIC-IV infusion orders are **split into segments**: the rows of one `linkorderid` follow each other in time and several drugs share a segment's start time. Crucially, a **re-ordered** row (`statusdescription` = `ChangeDose/Rate` / `Paused` / `Stopped`) carries the *previous* order's `originalamount`, so:

| duration source | infusion rows correct |
|---|---|
| `originalamount / (rate·weight·unit_factor)` (FinishedRunning) | 1005 / 1945 |
| same rule for re-ordered rows | **0 / 718** |
| **segment length** (next *distinct* start time of the same `linkorderid`) for re-ordered rows | **366 / 718** |

